---
layout: base.njk
title: Safety Framework
description: "The integrated safety framework covering Safety Domains, Organisational Drivers, System Enablers, and the Operating Environment."
---
<div class="wrap" style="padding-top:1.5rem;">
  <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/about/">About Sport Safety</a> / Safety Framework</p>
</div>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">About Sport Safety</span>
    <h1>Safety Framework</h1>
    <p class="lede">{{ safetyFramework.intro }}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap" style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:2.5rem; align-items:start;">
    <div>
      <h2>The Framework at a Glance</h2>
      <p>The framework is structured as four concentric layers, each building on the one within it:</p>
      <ol class="framework-layers">
        <li><strong>Safety — Vision, Mission &amp; Targets</strong> at the core.</li>
        <li><strong>Three Safety Domains</strong> — Sport Safety, Safe Sport, and Workplace Safety — define the scope of the organisation's safety responsibilities.</li>
        <li><strong>Six Organisational Drivers</strong> — Commitment, Culture, Competencies, Controls, Collaboration, and Communication — translate intent into practice.</li>
        <li><strong>Nine System Enablers</strong> provide the structures and processes that make the drivers work.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>All of this operates within the <strong>Operating Environment</strong> — the strategic, legal, and stakeholder context that shapes every decision.</p>
    </div>
    <img src="/assets/images/safety-framework.png" alt="Safety framework wheel diagram showing Safety Domains, Organisational Drivers, System Enablers, and Operating Environment" style="border-radius:8px; width:100%;">
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Three Safety Domains</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The three domains define the full scope of the organisation's safety responsibilities — they are interconnected and must be managed together.</p>
    <div class="grid-cards cols-3">
      {% for domain in safetyFramework.domains %}
        <div class="card">
          <h3>{{ domain.name }}</h3>
          <p>{{ domain.body }}</p>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Six Organisational Drivers</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The six drivers represent the dimensions of organisational safety practice that must be actively managed. Strength across all six is required for a mature safety system.</p>
    <div class="grid-cards cols-3">
      {% for driver in safetyFramework.drivers %}
        <div class="card pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-dot" style="background:{{ driver.colour }};"></div>
          <h3>{{ driver.name }}</h3>
          <p>{{ driver.body }}</p>
          <ul class="pillar-list">
            {% for el in driver.elements %}
              <li>{{ el }}</li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Nine System Enablers</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The system enablers are the organisational functions and processes that support the six drivers — providing structure, resources, and oversight.</p>
    <div class="grid-cards cols-3">
      {% for enabler in safetyFramework.enablers %}
        <div class="card">
          <h4>{{ enabler.name }}</h4>
          <p>{{ enabler.body }}</p>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Operating Environment</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The outer ring of the framework defines the broader environment within which all safety management activity takes place — the strategic, contextual, and legal boundaries that inform every layer within.</p>
    <div class="grid-cards cols-3">
      {% for item in safetyFramework.environment %}
        <div class="card">
          <h4>{{ item.name }}</h4>
          <p>{{ item.body }}</p>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Informing Standards</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The framework is informed by internationally recognised standards to ensure rigour, credibility, and alignment with global best practice.</p>
    <div class="grid-cards cols-2">
      {% for standard in safetyFramework.standards %}
        <div class="card">
          <h4>{{ standard.name }}</h4>
          <p>{{ standard.body }}</p>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="list-row"><span>Back to About Sport Safety</span><a class="link" href="/about/">About Sport Safety →</a></div>
    <div class="list-row"><span>Report a safety concern</span><a class="link" href="/report/">Report an Incident/Hazard →</a></div>
    <div class="list-row"><span>Explore safety resources</span><a class="link" href="/resources/">Safety Resources →</a></div>
  </div>
</section>
